Carl posted:
>Has anyone out there done the math on whether, given a desire for
>teleport control, it is more efficient to wish for a ring of teleport
>control or to reverse genocide tengu?

The game picks an intrinsic and then tries to give it to you. In the
case of tengu it picks from {PR,tele,TC} with 1/3 probability each.
Then it tries to give you that resistance with a probability of
level/weight. The level of a tengu is 6 and for most resistances
weight is 15 but for tele it is 10, and TC, 12. So we have

PR   1/3 * 6/15 = 2/15 ~ 13%
tele 1/3 * 6/10 =  1/5 = 20%
TC   1/3 * 6/12 =  1/6 ~ 17%

So from any given tengu corpse or tin you have a probability of
getting TC of about 17%.

This is independent of other factors. In particular the initial
intrinsic choice does not take into account the ones you have already
so there's no point in trying to contract teleportitis from something
else before eating tengu.

